# playpick cell: mode=raid boss=whisper spec=shaman:restoration style=mash
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=390x844,touch save=fresh.
#
# What is actually new here: no session on record has ever landed a raid-mode
# pull of The Last Whisper at all -- its four prior appearances in
# sessions.jsonl were mage:frost/auto (mode=clear, never reached it),
# priest:shadow/mash (mode=walk, wiped in THE VIGIL before ever reaching it),
# warrior:protection/idle and paladin:holy/idle (both mode=raid, but neither
# a healer nor mash). This is the first mash-style pull of this boss and the
# first shaman:restoration under mash anywhere. mash round-robins ability
# slots 1-5 with no movement at all (scripts/playbot.ts: mash is absent from
# every steering branch), so a healer under mash stands still on the spot it
# spawns and randomly casts heals and fillers alike with no target logic of
# its own -- a different shape of "does nothing useful" than [[#1]]'s idle
# entries, which never press anything at all. The room's own demand is "cut
# the shard, swap the hold, and hold off your own" (src/sim/encounters.ts) --
# a straight-line-mechanic room, the first non-round arena in the game -- so
# standing on one spot for the whole fight is a real test of whether this
# room punishes not moving the way a round room does not.
#
# whisper is tier 0 of its own wing on the chain and a fresh save opens
# nothing above Bonegrinder 10-normal, so #b=whisper&s=10&h=0 (h=0 normal)
# is the direct-link recipe every raid-mode session on an unlocked-later
# boss has used.

